DEPENDENCY DEFERRAL — why the two xcodebuild scheme steps are DEFERRED (not green)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REPRODUCED (not assumed). Building the app target on this host fails deterministically:

  $ xcodebuild -project TeslaSync.xcodeproj -target TeslaSync -sdk iphonesimulator build
  error: There is no XCFramework found at
         '.../apps/apple/Frameworks/Shared.xcframework'. (in target 'TeslaSync')
  BUILD_RESULT=65

The TeslaSync iOS/macOS app targets link the KMP `Shared.xcframework` (ADR-004). Staging it
requires the Kotlin/Native Apple toolchain via `apps/shared/gradlew :core:assembleSharedXCFramework`
(a scheme pre-build phase). `apps/macos-pending-verifications.md` explicitly defers this artifact to
the `macos-latest` CI runners (origin S3-0001 → H8-0001 / P99-0001). An attempt to stage it here ran
> 13 min with no artifact under heavy concurrent Gradle-daemon load from the sibling parallel slots
sharing this host, and was stopped to avoid disrupting co-tenant builds. This is a pre-existing,
environment/integration dependency — NOT a defect in this surface.

Scope note: in this slot `struct DashboardWidgetSize` / `DashboardWidgetRegistration` is defined
exactly ONCE (Sources/DashboardWidgets/DashboardWidgetInfra.swift) — the historical cross-slot
duplicate-symbol blocker does not apply here. ChargeCostTrackerWidget.* adds no redefinition.
Per project.yml the co-located *Tests.swift are excluded from the app target and compiled only into
the XCTest bundles, so they introduce no app-target import of XCTest.

Net: the full-app `xcodebuild build test` is DEFERRED to the signed macos-latest acceptance gate
(P99-0001), matching the disposition of all 60 sibling P4 dashboard-widget surfaces. The surface
itself is proven GREEN by [B]/[C]/[D] against the real design system + Swift 6 strict concurrency.

